  "answer_text": "For the CMA side of the BGP Session Disconnected playbook: to find the disconnect reason, use the CMA Events page (Home > Events) with the BGP peers disconnected preset; this shows a history of BGP disconnect events and provides a BGP Disconnect Error Code. To verify the route table, use the CMA Routing Table view (Monitoring > Routing Table); it lists all routes (including BGP routes, which appear as Dynamic), enabling you to confirm how routes are being advertised and which tunnel is affected.",
